1
00:00:05,272 --> 00:00:07,140
FINAL EPISODE

2
00:00:09,843 --> 00:00:13,313
Doctor, what's wrong with him?

3
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:17,317
We need the test results to be sure,
but it's obvious without looking.

4
00:00:17,384 --> 00:00:20,287
Why didn't you hospitalize
a man in this condition?

5
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:22,289
Hospitalize him?

6
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:23,757
Why?

7
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:26,493
Should I beat around the bush
and keep it vague,

8
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:29,930
or give it to you straight?

9
00:00:29,997 --> 00:00:32,199
Well, give it to me straight…

10
00:00:32,266 --> 00:00:36,003
It's cancer. Cancer. Liver cancer.
And it's terminal.

11
00:00:36,069 --> 00:00:39,006
I treated this patient back in Seoul.

12
00:00:40,007 --> 00:00:41,808
Oh…

13
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:43,610
He has cancer?

14
00:00:44,278 --> 00:00:45,679
What do you mean…

15
00:00:45,746 --> 00:00:49,583
He was already diagnosed as terminal
some time ago.

16
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:52,619
Up to a year, six months on average,
as little as three.

17
00:00:52,686 --> 00:00:54,655
But since his time has run out now,

18
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,858
it wouldn't be surprising
if he died this very day.

19
00:00:58,792 --> 00:01:02,930
He's… dying?

20
00:01:11,638 --> 00:01:15,208
Su-yeon, where am I?

21
00:01:16,777 --> 00:01:19,580
Su-yeon, what's wrong?

22
00:01:20,981 --> 00:01:23,517
Doctor, what are you doing here…

23
00:01:23,584 --> 00:01:27,287
Should I beat around the bush
or give it to you straight?

24
00:01:29,389 --> 00:01:33,293
I got busted pocketing kickbacks
from a drug company.

25
00:01:34,061 --> 00:01:36,863
I got treated at a hostess bar.
The director came in.

26
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:41,234
I should've played dumb,
denied it, flat-out denied it.

27
00:01:41,301 --> 00:01:43,503
I just spilled it all straight out.

28
00:01:43,570 --> 00:01:46,173
So I got exiled to the countryside.

29
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:50,911
Even with yourself, Doctor,
you just keep it straight,

30
00:01:50,978 --> 00:01:54,715
throwing fastballs left and right.

31
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:55,949
You know how I am.

32
00:01:56,016 --> 00:01:58,585
It's exhausting. Really exhausting.

33
00:02:02,356 --> 00:02:04,625
Doctor, the test results are in.

34
00:02:04,691 --> 00:02:05,959
They are?

35
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,328
Just wait a moment.

36
00:02:11,198 --> 00:02:12,566
The test results…

37
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:16,703
Su-yeon, let's go. Um…

38
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:18,505
I think I have to go.

39
00:02:18,572 --> 00:02:21,942
I had something to do.
It's fine to take this out, right?

40
00:02:22,709 --> 00:02:25,779
No, um… I'm really fine.

41
00:02:25,846 --> 00:02:29,249
I didn't eat yesterday,
so I just got dizzy and fainted.

42
00:02:29,316 --> 00:02:31,351
The test results will say the same.

43
00:02:31,418 --> 00:02:33,487
Hurry, let's get out. Hurry, let's go!

44
00:02:35,188 --> 00:02:36,356
Su-yeon, let's go eat.

45
00:02:36,423 --> 00:02:38,291
I'm starving to death.

46
00:02:38,358 --> 00:02:40,560
Being this hungry makes a guy faint.

47
00:02:40,627 --> 00:02:41,995
In this day and age,

48
00:02:42,062 --> 00:02:44,297
who just keels over like that?

49
00:02:48,735 --> 00:02:50,070
What's wrong?

50
00:02:51,405 --> 00:02:54,107
-How long will you keep lying to me?
-What?

51
00:02:54,775 --> 00:02:55,809
You have cancer?

52
00:02:55,876 --> 00:02:58,578
And I heard it's terminal!

53
00:02:58,645 --> 00:03:02,482
Um, Su-yeon, how did you…

54
00:03:02,549 --> 00:03:03,417
Uh, well…

55
00:03:03,483 --> 00:03:05,285
The doctor told me everything.

56
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:09,456
Why didn't you tell me? Why lie to me?

57
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,494
I'm sorry.

58
00:03:14,561 --> 00:03:16,596
Is saying sorry enough?

59
00:03:16,663 --> 00:03:20,233
You think you can stay silent
and just pass away all alone?

60
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,569
Then what about me?

61
00:03:23,303 --> 00:03:26,206
What am I supposed to do then?

62
00:03:34,314 --> 00:03:39,319
What? So money was buried
in your cabbage patch?

63
00:03:39,386 --> 00:03:41,555
And five billion won in cash?

64
00:03:43,190 --> 00:03:47,594
Gosh, we had no clue
and just grew cabbages for months.

65
00:03:47,661 --> 00:03:50,897
But Su-yeon is mind-blowing.
What a total plot twist.

66
00:03:50,964 --> 00:03:52,899
I know, with that innocent face.

67
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:55,168
How could she hatch such an evil plot?

68
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:58,839
Anyway, when will we ever
sell cabbages and release an album?

69
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:01,074
Seeing 5 billion in cash
with my own eyes

70
00:04:01,141 --> 00:04:03,410
just kills all my motivation to work.

71
00:04:03,477 --> 00:04:05,912
Right, the camcorder!

72
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:08,915
Guys, don't worry.

73
00:04:08,982 --> 00:04:12,018
I've got a good idea.

74
00:04:15,655 --> 00:04:17,090
Jackpot, jackpot, jackpot!

75
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:22,829
Freeze!

76
00:04:24,865 --> 00:04:26,933
Why are you doing this?

77
00:04:27,634 --> 00:04:29,770
Hands up! Don't move!

78
00:04:39,079 --> 00:04:40,947
Hello?

79
00:04:41,014 --> 00:04:42,516
Is this the TV station?

80
00:04:47,187 --> 00:04:49,356
Su-yeon, please stop crying.

81
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:52,459
Still, seeing you cry for me

82
00:04:52,526 --> 00:04:53,927
makes me feel so good.

83
00:04:55,829 --> 00:04:57,631
Is this any time to be joking?

84
00:04:57,697 --> 00:04:59,866
I'm not joking.

85
00:05:01,535 --> 00:05:04,004
Watching you, Su-yeon,

86
00:05:04,938 --> 00:05:07,574
I was truly happy.

87
00:05:07,641 --> 00:05:10,110
I had no hope at all,

88
00:05:10,177 --> 00:05:13,780
but seeing you, I held on and held on.

89
00:05:14,548 --> 00:05:17,184
No matter how painful and hard it was,

90
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:19,352
just looking at you

91
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:23,390
gave me strength and brought me joy.

92
00:05:26,126 --> 00:05:28,161
And until the very end,

93
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:32,332
you gave me good memories
to take with me when I go.

94
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,001
Thank you.

95
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:41,041
All my life, no, even after I die,

96
00:05:41,107 --> 00:05:42,976
I will never forget you.

97
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:50,317
Su-yeon, it's cold. Please go inside.

98
00:05:50,917 --> 00:05:53,920
And please keep this
a secret from my friends.

99
00:05:55,155 --> 00:05:57,958
Those guys may seem like nutcases,

100
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:01,761
but they care deeply and cry easily.

101
00:06:03,964 --> 00:06:06,833
I'll be on my way, then.

102
00:06:17,544 --> 00:06:20,180
Hey, where have you been?

103
00:06:20,247 --> 00:06:23,617
The landlady told us to pack and leave.

104
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:28,054
What's wrong? Are you crying?

105
00:06:29,089 --> 00:06:31,024
Hwa-ran.

106
00:06:31,791 --> 00:06:35,962
What do I do? What do I do?

107
00:06:37,464 --> 00:06:39,532
Han-cheol…

108
00:06:41,468 --> 00:06:44,170
-Han-cheol…
-What about that weirdo?

109
00:06:48,541 --> 00:06:50,577
Hwa-ran.

110
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:54,080
That weirdo, I really…

111
00:06:54,147 --> 00:06:57,350
I think I really liked him.

112
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:27,314
Anyway, has our village's luck run out?

113
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:31,051
A meteorite, now a slush fund.
All kinds of crazy things happen.

114
00:07:31,117 --> 00:07:33,386
I know. There's never a quiet day here.

115
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:35,822
-Exactly.
-Guys!

116
00:07:35,889 --> 00:07:38,358
-Hello.
-What brings you here?

117
00:07:38,425 --> 00:07:40,493
Turn on the news! Hurry!

118
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,329
Why the news all of a sudden?

119
00:07:42,395 --> 00:07:44,564
Please, just turn it on!

120
00:07:44,631 --> 00:07:46,266
Well, this is strange.

121
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:48,101
Goodness.

122
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:50,971
It just started!

123
00:07:51,037 --> 00:07:52,539
Watch this very closely!

124
00:07:52,605 --> 00:07:53,707
It's News 20 Years.

125
00:07:53,773 --> 00:07:55,208
Here is our top story.

126
00:07:55,275 --> 00:07:56,142
In the area,

127
00:07:56,209 --> 00:07:59,012
BREAKING: ASSEMBLYMAN
KIM SEONG-JU'S SLUSH FUND FOUND

128
00:08:01,348 --> 00:08:04,184
It is likely Assemblyman
Kim Seong-ju's slush fund,

129
00:08:04,250 --> 00:08:07,020
but Assemblyman Kim Seong-ju
strongly denies it.

130
00:08:07,087 --> 00:08:10,590
Amid heated debate over
who owns this slush fund,

131
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:12,892
an anonymous tipster today

132
00:08:12,959 --> 00:08:17,297
sent us crucial evidence showing
the entire scene intact.

133
00:08:17,364 --> 00:08:19,833
We will now reveal it to you.

134
00:08:23,370 --> 00:08:25,538
Hey, why are we on there?

135
00:08:26,306 --> 00:08:27,173
I know.

136
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:30,777
And why are we on for so long?
We're not even part of the case.

137
00:08:32,145 --> 00:08:33,113
Freeze! Stop!

138
00:08:33,913 --> 00:08:35,015
That's a fake gun.

139
00:08:35,081 --> 00:08:36,950
-It's fake?
-That's right.

140
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:39,586
I thought he really shot Ki-jun dead.

141
00:08:39,652 --> 00:08:41,154
You punk!

142
00:08:41,721 --> 00:08:42,589
Get rid of him!

143
00:08:42,655 --> 00:08:44,224
He's the worst of the worst.

144
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:45,725
This is decisive footage.

145
00:08:45,792 --> 00:08:48,561
Will Assemblyman Kim Seong-ju
still feign innocence?

146
00:08:48,628 --> 00:08:50,363
We are quite curious to see.

147
00:08:50,430 --> 00:08:52,298
Now for our next story.

148
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:54,267
My goodness.

149
00:08:54,334 --> 00:08:55,402
What do you think?

150
00:08:55,468 --> 00:08:56,336
Amazing, right?

151
00:08:56,403 --> 00:08:59,539
I tell you, the camcorder
caught the whole crime scene!

152
00:08:59,606 --> 00:09:01,007
I see.

153
00:09:01,074 --> 00:09:03,009
Hey, why was our song playing?

154
00:09:03,076 --> 00:09:05,545
That was my condition for the footage.

155
00:09:06,446 --> 00:09:08,715
-Why?
-You goldfish! Total goldfish!

156
00:09:08,782 --> 00:09:11,918
If our nine o'clock main news
airs that key footage

157
00:09:11,985 --> 00:09:13,486
with your faces and song,

158
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,355
is that good publicity or not?

159
00:09:15,422 --> 00:09:17,524
Besides, will it only air here?

160
00:09:17,590 --> 00:09:19,726
On the three major networks, cable,

161
00:09:19,793 --> 00:09:21,561
plus online videos and all that,

162
00:09:21,628 --> 00:09:24,097
your song will ring out everywhere!

163
00:09:24,864 --> 00:09:26,533
Oh, so our faces got on TV

164
00:09:26,599 --> 00:09:28,201
giving us real publicity now,

165
00:09:28,268 --> 00:09:30,336
so now, now our pickled cabbage

166
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,906
is bound to sell like crazy!

167
00:09:32,972 --> 00:09:36,576
Are you an idiot? A dolphin?
Is cabbage what matters right now?

168
00:09:36,643 --> 00:09:38,378
You could become stars, stars!

169
00:09:38,445 --> 00:09:41,648
Stars? Give me a break.
Hey, do you think that'll happen?

170
00:09:41,714 --> 00:09:44,150
I just hope our cabbages sell well now.

171
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:49,489
Huh? We're on the trending searches.

172
00:09:49,556 --> 00:09:51,925
-Already?
-Modern Farmer is fifth.

173
00:09:51,991 --> 00:09:54,294
Seventh is the Hadurok-ri slush fund.

174
00:09:55,328 --> 00:09:57,030
Come on, what are you doing?

175
00:09:58,832 --> 00:10:00,400
Hello? Yes, what is it?

176
00:10:00,467 --> 00:10:01,534
Yes, what is it?

177
00:10:02,769 --> 00:10:03,736
Yes.

178
00:10:04,971 --> 00:10:06,406
An interview?

179
00:10:07,373 --> 00:10:09,042
Yes, sure.

180
00:10:09,109 --> 00:10:10,176
Okay.

181
00:10:10,597 --> 00:10:11,778
An interview?

182
00:10:11,845 --> 00:10:13,947
See? What did I tell you?

183
00:10:14,013 --> 00:10:15,748
Life turns around in one shot!

184
00:10:15,815 --> 00:10:18,651
Hey, then let's use this chance

185
00:10:18,718 --> 00:10:21,921
to really promote
our pickled cabbage, huh? Right?

186
00:10:21,988 --> 00:10:24,190
Yes, yes, bro!
Let's sell pickled cabbage!

187
00:10:24,257 --> 00:10:26,059
We'll sell out. It's a done deal.

188
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:28,795
Everyone already, already
knows our pickled cabbage!

189
00:10:30,196 --> 00:10:32,832
This, this pickled cabbage
is in the shot, right?

190
00:10:33,933 --> 00:10:35,768
Yes, we're getting a good shot.

191
00:10:35,835 --> 00:10:37,337
Let's begin the interview.

192
00:10:37,403 --> 00:10:39,539
As the hero of this slush fund case,

193
00:10:39,606 --> 00:10:41,508
how do you feel right now?

194
00:10:41,574 --> 00:10:44,244
Well… how do I feel right now?

195
00:10:44,944 --> 00:10:48,915
In short, I would like to say this.

196
00:10:48,982 --> 00:10:52,152
Life is much like a cabbage.

197
00:10:53,386 --> 00:10:56,656
At times, snails may appear,

198
00:10:56,723 --> 00:10:58,791
and water deer may appear too.

199
00:10:59,292 --> 00:11:02,328
But if you endure and press on,

200
00:11:02,395 --> 00:11:04,531
you can harvest cabbages like these.

201
00:11:04,597 --> 00:11:07,400
So, um, these harvested cabbages

202
00:11:07,467 --> 00:11:12,772
finally become tasty pickled cabbage.
Well, something like that, yes…

203
00:11:13,406 --> 00:11:17,777
Oh, um, yes. By the way,
I heard you used to be in a band.

204
00:11:17,844 --> 00:11:20,480
How did you end up growing cabbages?

205
00:11:21,247 --> 00:11:25,218
Um… Actually, after our band broke up,

206
00:11:25,285 --> 00:11:27,253
I truly lived like a loser.

207
00:11:28,054 --> 00:11:32,692
With no dreams and no hope,
I spent every single day like that.

208
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:37,764
Then one day, I saw the charm
of this pickled cabbage

209
00:11:37,830 --> 00:11:39,232
and fell deeply in love!

210
00:11:39,299 --> 00:11:41,301
Tightly packed, top-grade cabbage!

211
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:42,869
Crunchy texture, nutritious!

212
00:11:42,936 --> 00:11:45,205
Hadurok-ri pickled cabbage is the best!

213
00:11:45,271 --> 00:11:47,840
-It's the best!
-Well, that's our story.

214
00:11:49,342 --> 00:11:51,244
Oh… Uh, yes.

215
00:11:52,812 --> 00:11:55,181
Hey, Ki-jun, you spoke so well today.

216
00:11:55,248 --> 00:11:56,316
Hey, you did great.

217
00:11:56,382 --> 00:11:58,418
Come on, I can't compare to you.

218
00:12:00,053 --> 00:12:02,789
Pickled cabbage orders really shot up!

219
00:12:02,855 --> 00:12:04,791
Right, we're still trending online.

220
00:12:04,857 --> 00:12:07,660
The power of TV is just incredible!

221
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:11,631
Even so, we have a long way to go
to save up enough for our album.

222
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,068
What's with your face?

223
00:12:15,134 --> 00:12:17,036
Things are going great. What's up?

224
00:12:17,103 --> 00:12:18,905
No, no, it's nothing.

225
00:12:20,473 --> 00:12:23,109
Oh? Hi, Yu-na.

226
00:12:23,176 --> 00:12:25,078
Hello.

227
00:12:25,144 --> 00:12:27,213
I'm sorry for deceiving you until now.

228
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,982
Not at all, it's okay.

229
00:12:29,048 --> 00:12:30,717
You didn't do us any harm.

230
00:12:30,783 --> 00:12:32,452
Thank you for understanding.

231
00:12:32,518 --> 00:12:36,422
Um, I'm sorry, but
could I borrow Han-cheol for a day?

232
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:40,059
-What?
-What would you use him for?

233
00:12:40,893 --> 00:12:42,462
Let us go on a date.

234
00:12:42,528 --> 00:12:44,497
All right!

235
00:12:46,065 --> 00:12:48,167
-Hey, stop it.
-Oh, come on.

236
00:12:48,234 --> 00:12:49,435
Sure, go on ahead.

237
00:12:49,502 --> 00:12:52,739
I'll give you the day off
from cabbage-pickling hell.

238
00:12:53,539 --> 00:12:55,575
Thank you.

239
00:12:55,642 --> 00:12:57,844
-Han-cheol.
-Hey, will you be okay?

240
00:12:57,910 --> 00:13:00,546
Um, Su-yeon, why are you doing this?

241
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:03,249
Please pickle our gorilla deep in love!

242
00:13:03,316 --> 00:13:06,653
Oh, nice! Have a great time, you two!

243
00:13:12,592 --> 00:13:16,629
What should we do after coffee?
A movie? An amusement park?

244
00:13:17,930 --> 00:13:21,067
Why do this all of a sudden, Su-yeon?
You're scaring me.

245
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,835
We don't have much time.

246
00:13:22,902 --> 00:13:25,238
We should do it all while we have time.

247
00:13:25,305 --> 00:13:27,273
Han-cheol, anything you wanted to do?

248
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,742
I'll do it all with you. Tell me.

249
00:13:29,809 --> 00:13:30,910
There's nothing.

250
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:33,646
You must've thought of something once.

251
00:13:33,713 --> 00:13:36,049
Really nothing? Really? For real?

252
00:13:36,115 --> 00:13:38,017
Um, could you let go first, then?

253
00:13:39,419 --> 00:13:41,854
Then let's just have coffee
and go home.

254
00:13:41,921 --> 00:13:45,124
Uh, why are you getting so upset?

255
00:13:45,191 --> 00:13:49,028
I do have something. It's just, um…

256
00:13:49,729 --> 00:13:51,664
What is it?

257
00:13:51,731 --> 00:13:53,700
I wrote it down in my notes here.

258
00:13:53,766 --> 00:13:55,835
What is this?

259
00:13:57,870 --> 00:13:59,939
Bucket list?

260
00:14:00,473 --> 00:14:03,943
Come on, you even made a whole list!

261
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,812
BUCKET LIST

262
00:14:08,614 --> 00:14:13,586
But except for number one,
everything is about a girlfriend.

263
00:14:14,287 --> 00:14:19,625
I've never had a girlfriend, not once.

264
00:14:19,692 --> 00:14:23,563
I see. Time's short, so let's start!

265
00:14:24,263 --> 00:14:29,001
We already went on a date
in matching outfits last time.

266
00:14:29,068 --> 00:14:32,638
Number three, getting couple rings.

267
00:14:34,907 --> 00:14:36,509
Come on, get up.

268
00:14:36,576 --> 00:14:40,346
-Where are we going?
-To get our couple rings, of course.

269
00:14:44,350 --> 00:14:46,386
Um, excuse me.

270
00:14:46,452 --> 00:14:49,422
Yes? And who are you?

271
00:14:49,489 --> 00:14:51,124
Yes, hello.

272
00:14:51,190 --> 00:14:55,661
I am Yoon Seok-ho,
Head of Planning at Hanseong Music.

273
00:14:55,728 --> 00:14:59,532
You are the members
of Modern Farmer, right?

274
00:14:59,599 --> 00:15:00,867
Yes, we are. Why?

275
00:15:00,933 --> 00:15:03,870
Well, I have something to tell you.

276
00:15:03,936 --> 00:15:06,139
Could we move somewhere else to talk?

277
00:15:06,205 --> 00:15:10,009
We're busy salting cabbages right now.

278
00:15:10,076 --> 00:15:11,277
Can you tell us here?

279
00:15:11,344 --> 00:15:13,479
All right, we can do that.

280
00:15:14,313 --> 00:15:16,916
To get straight to the point,

281
00:15:17,850 --> 00:15:19,218
I want to sign a contract.

282
00:15:19,285 --> 00:15:21,287
What?

283
00:15:21,354 --> 00:15:22,388
A contract?

284
00:15:22,455 --> 00:15:25,191
Yes, our CEO was watching the news

285
00:15:25,258 --> 00:15:27,427
and apparently heard you all singing.

286
00:15:27,493 --> 00:15:29,228
They said the song was so good.

287
00:15:29,295 --> 00:15:31,063
They pestered me to sign you fast,

288
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:32,532
so I rushed down here.

289
00:15:33,332 --> 00:15:35,902
Our CEO is extremely impatient.

290
00:15:37,069 --> 00:15:39,672
You really want a contract with us?

291
00:15:39,739 --> 00:15:41,874
Yes, we want to sign you right away

292
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:44,677
and produce an album. What do you say?

293
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,250
Hello, CEO.

294
00:15:51,818 --> 00:15:53,953
Excuse me while I take this call.

295
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:55,688
Yes, sure.

296
00:15:56,322 --> 00:15:58,157
A recording studio?

297
00:15:58,224 --> 00:15:59,225
We must sign first.

298
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:01,561
We must sign first to book a studio.

299
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:03,963
Pinch me. Come on, pinch me.

300
00:16:04,030 --> 00:16:06,966
Ow! That hurts, it hurts!

301
00:16:07,033 --> 00:16:08,401
This isn't a lie, is it?

302
00:16:08,468 --> 00:16:10,670
Are we really making an album? Are we?

303
00:16:23,850 --> 00:16:25,651
I'm sorry.

304
00:16:25,718 --> 00:16:28,788
Why are couple rings so darn pricey?

305
00:16:28,855 --> 00:16:31,324
Once we get money,
let's get nice ones, us two.

306
00:16:31,390 --> 00:16:33,426
It's fine. This is plenty pretty.

307
00:16:33,493 --> 00:16:36,329
I love it. Honestly, it's so pretty.

308
00:16:37,296 --> 00:16:41,234
We got couple rings. What was next?

309
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:44,303
1. TELL MOM I LOVE HER
2. DATE IN MATCHING OUTFITS

310
00:16:44,370 --> 00:16:47,039
3. GET COUPLE RINGS 4. KISS

311
00:16:47,106 --> 00:16:49,208
Um… It's a kiss.

312
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:54,180
We don't have time,
so let's do this on a trip next time.

313
00:16:54,247 --> 00:16:57,517
Han-cheol, where should we go?
The beach? The mountains?

314
00:16:58,351 --> 00:17:00,319
Where would be nice?

315
00:17:02,889 --> 00:17:05,224
Su-yeon.

316
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:08,861
Let's stop now.

317
00:17:08,928 --> 00:17:10,963
What? Stop what?

318
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,232
From here on.

319
00:17:15,334 --> 00:17:19,705
Do the rest with a better man later.

320
00:17:22,308 --> 00:17:26,812
Another man? What do you mean by that?

321
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:29,949
Do you really not know what I mean?

322
00:17:31,350 --> 00:17:33,920
Su-yeon, if you keep doing this…

323
00:17:36,155 --> 00:17:40,826
I just want to live more and more.

324
00:17:46,766 --> 00:17:48,801
At first, Su-yeon,

325
00:17:48,868 --> 00:17:51,237
I only hoped you'd like me back.

326
00:17:51,304 --> 00:17:56,475
But now that you like me, I regret it.

327
00:17:57,677 --> 00:17:59,312
Why?

328
00:18:01,213 --> 00:18:03,849
Later on, when I'm dead and gone,

329
00:18:05,418 --> 00:18:07,453
you'll cry again, Su-yeon.

330
00:18:09,388 --> 00:18:12,291
Then who will be by your side?

331
00:18:12,358 --> 00:18:15,127
If you catch a cold later, Su-yeon,

332
00:18:15,194 --> 00:18:17,964
who will be there to take care of you?

333
00:18:19,465 --> 00:18:22,501
I wish I had never fallen for you.

334
00:18:26,205 --> 00:18:29,875
No, Han-cheol. Because you liked me,

335
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:33,846
I was so glad and happy.

336
00:18:37,783 --> 00:18:39,719
I really mean it.

337
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:44,090
I gaze at you

338
00:18:44,657 --> 00:18:47,093
I wait only for you

339
00:18:47,159 --> 00:18:50,229
Always in the same spot

340
00:18:50,296 --> 00:18:52,999
In the same place

341
00:18:54,667 --> 00:18:58,070
Even when I miss you like crazy

342
00:18:58,137 --> 00:19:01,707
Even when I long for you like crazy

343
00:19:12,385 --> 00:19:16,055
How did it go?
Still haven't found that patient?

344
00:19:16,122 --> 00:19:19,825
No, sir. His contact info
isn't properly listed on the chart,

345
00:19:19,892 --> 00:19:21,761
so it's really hard to find him.

346
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:24,263
Still, it's really strange.

347
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:26,766
How could he improve so suddenly?

348
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:28,234
He was clearly terminal.

349
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:31,370
At this rate, he could be fully cured.

350
00:19:31,437 --> 00:19:33,072
This is a miracle. A miracle!

351
00:19:34,306 --> 00:19:38,678
Why'd this guy run out of the hospital?

352
00:19:38,744 --> 00:19:41,614
He's not off bawling
and making a scene again, is he?

353
00:19:57,997 --> 00:19:59,498
Smile brightly

354
00:19:59,565 --> 00:20:01,500
If you were to ask me

355
00:20:02,101 --> 00:20:05,104
what my sin is,

356
00:20:09,542 --> 00:20:14,013
meeting this woman, loving her,

357
00:20:15,047 --> 00:20:19,285
and leaving her behind alone
would be my greatest sin.

358
00:20:25,458 --> 00:20:27,326
Su-yeon.

359
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:30,196
I have a favor to ask you.

360
00:20:31,997 --> 00:20:33,032
What is it?

361
00:20:33,099 --> 00:20:35,534
Please go back to Seoul.

362
00:20:36,202 --> 00:20:38,938
And forget a guy like me and move on.

363
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:42,041
Never contact me again.

364
00:20:42,108 --> 00:20:44,977
Don't come looking for me.

365
00:20:45,044 --> 00:20:47,613
And don't even think about me.

366
00:20:49,348 --> 00:20:52,885
And in the next life…

367
00:20:55,087 --> 00:20:57,189
let's be sure to meet again.

368
00:20:58,290 --> 00:20:59,592
Han-cheol!

369
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:04,697
Su-yeon, in the next life,
let's be sure to meet again.

370
00:21:06,632 --> 00:21:08,968
No, I refuse.

371
00:21:09,034 --> 00:21:12,571
I can't let you go like this.
I can never let you go.

372
00:21:12,638 --> 00:21:13,939
Let's get you treated.

373
00:21:14,006 --> 00:21:17,376
You know as well as I do
that it's already too late.

374
00:21:17,443 --> 00:21:20,379
A miracle could still happen.

375
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:22,815
Let's try our best together.

376
00:21:22,882 --> 00:21:24,950
I'm begging you, Han-cheol.

377
00:21:27,353 --> 00:21:29,822
Su-yeon, Su-yeon.

378
00:21:29,889 --> 00:21:31,891
Han-cheol!

379
00:21:47,106 --> 00:21:48,874
Here, have a drink, everyone.

380
00:21:49,441 --> 00:21:53,412
After we had nothing but rotten luck,

381
00:21:53,479 --> 00:21:55,181
what in the world is this?

382
00:21:55,247 --> 00:21:57,917
So you're becoming a real singer now?

383
00:21:57,983 --> 00:22:02,154
I told you! The CEO is going crazy
to put an album out fast, just crazy!

384
00:22:03,422 --> 00:22:05,024
Then you'll be on TV now.

385
00:22:05,090 --> 00:22:05,958
Congrats!

386
00:22:06,025 --> 00:22:07,993
Thanks, kid.

387
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:10,629
Never forget this is all thanks to me.

388
00:22:10,696 --> 00:22:13,432
Yes, I shall not forget
your grace for all my days.

389
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:17,770
Okay, so when are you heading up?

390
00:22:19,038 --> 00:22:21,140
I'll go up once I wrap things up here.

391
00:22:21,207 --> 00:22:24,810
So it'll be hard to see you guys here.

392
00:22:27,246 --> 00:22:28,948
Can't you stay?

393
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:32,885
I told you I'd come visit often.

394
00:22:32,952 --> 00:22:35,955
Then promise me.

395
00:22:36,021 --> 00:22:41,126
Okay, I'll come visit
at least once a week. Promise.

396
00:22:41,927 --> 00:22:43,596
Promise.

397
00:22:53,806 --> 00:22:56,008
You're checking into the hospital now

398
00:22:56,075 --> 00:22:59,144
and starting treatment, got it?

399
00:23:00,946 --> 00:23:03,315
I'll stay right by your side,

400
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:05,217
so don't be afraid.

401
00:23:07,419 --> 00:23:11,390
Um, Su-yeon,
I'd like to stop by the barbershop.

402
00:23:11,457 --> 00:23:13,692
Why are you going to the barbershop?

403
00:23:13,759 --> 00:23:18,230
Once I start chemo, I'll lose my hair.

404
00:23:18,297 --> 00:23:20,933
I'm afraid seeing that
will make you sad again,

405
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,068
so I'd like to cut my hair first.

406
00:23:23,135 --> 00:23:24,436
Han-cheol.

407
00:23:24,503 --> 00:23:26,538
I'm doing this because I want to.

408
00:23:26,605 --> 00:23:28,274
That's okay, right?

409
00:23:34,847 --> 00:23:37,416
All right, how would you like it cut?

410
00:23:39,518 --> 00:23:42,254
Please shave it bald.
Not a single hair left.

411
00:23:42,321 --> 00:23:45,791
You want to shave it bald in winter?

412
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:47,593
You'll be cold.

413
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:50,729
Please don't ask anything
and just shave it bald.

414
00:23:50,796 --> 00:23:51,664
I'll be fine.

415
00:23:51,730 --> 00:23:53,365
All right, then.

416
00:23:54,934 --> 00:23:59,505
Holding you only in my heart

417
00:24:31,337 --> 00:24:33,172
Oh, miss!

418
00:24:33,973 --> 00:24:36,775
You're the young woman
I saw at the hospital, right?

419
00:24:36,842 --> 00:24:38,210
Um… Doctor.

420
00:24:38,277 --> 00:24:40,179
But why are you crying?

421
00:24:40,245 --> 00:24:43,682
More importantly, where's that patient?

422
00:24:44,249 --> 00:24:46,118
Why do you ask?

423
00:24:46,685 --> 00:24:49,121
His test results came back…

424
00:24:49,188 --> 00:24:50,923
and it's a miracle! A miracle!

425
00:24:50,990 --> 00:24:53,025
What?

426
00:24:53,092 --> 00:24:55,728
What do you mean, a miracle?

427
00:24:58,130 --> 00:25:00,666
What? His condition improved?

428
00:25:00,733 --> 00:25:02,701
I'm telling you, it did.

429
00:25:02,768 --> 00:25:04,503
It was terminal just months ago.

430
00:25:04,570 --> 00:25:06,705
I don't know why, but it improved.

431
00:25:06,772 --> 00:25:09,341
He could even be cured with treatment.

432
00:25:09,408 --> 00:25:10,709
Really?

433
00:25:10,776 --> 00:25:13,112
Thank you. Thank you so much.

434
00:25:13,178 --> 00:25:15,881
I didn't really do anything.

435
00:25:15,948 --> 00:25:18,083
But where is that patient right now?

436
00:25:18,150 --> 00:25:19,752
Afraid he'd do something rash,

437
00:25:19,818 --> 00:25:21,320
I was so worried about him.

438
00:25:21,387 --> 00:25:23,222
Where is that young man?

439
00:25:23,288 --> 00:25:24,857
He's in this barbershop.

440
00:25:26,792 --> 00:25:29,461
Wait! Oh, no, he can't do that!

441
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:31,230
Su-yeon, I just shaved my head.

442
00:25:33,065 --> 00:25:36,135
Doctor, what brings you here?

443
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:41,273
Han-cheol, um… well, you see.

444
00:25:43,509 --> 00:25:45,477
Your condition has improved.

445
00:25:47,112 --> 00:25:50,315
-Is that really true?
-I'm telling you, it is.

446
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:54,887
What did you do to get so much better?

447
00:25:54,953 --> 00:25:56,922
All I did was grow cabbages.

448
00:25:57,556 --> 00:25:58,824
Eat any special food?

449
00:25:59,425 --> 00:26:02,227
I just chewed on a lot of raw cabbage.

450
00:26:02,294 --> 00:26:04,530
Among terminal cancer patients,

451
00:26:04,596 --> 00:26:07,066
many are cured with natural remedies.

452
00:26:07,132 --> 00:26:10,002
They breathe fresh air
and eat organic food.

453
00:26:10,069 --> 00:26:12,037
You must be one of those cases.

454
00:26:12,104 --> 00:26:14,473
Thank you, Doctor! Thank you!

455
00:26:14,540 --> 00:26:16,642
You're not fully cured yet.

456
00:26:16,708 --> 00:26:18,243
Be sure to come in tomorrow.

457
00:26:18,310 --> 00:26:20,145
Yes.

458
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:24,083
But why did you shave your head?

459
00:26:25,317 --> 00:26:28,353
Oh, right! Oh, right!

460
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:30,322
Jeez, uh… you could've told me

461
00:26:30,389 --> 00:26:33,292
a little sooner, Doctor.

462
00:26:34,026 --> 00:26:36,462
My poor hair, seriously.

463
00:26:38,063 --> 00:26:39,965
We're already here.

464
00:26:40,032 --> 00:26:41,400
That's such a shame.

465
00:26:41,467 --> 00:26:43,102
Come on, hurry up.

466
00:26:46,205 --> 00:26:47,539
I'm just kidding.

467
00:26:47,606 --> 00:26:49,708
Still, it really is a shame.

468
00:26:51,810 --> 00:26:54,546
By the way, how long will it take?

469
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:56,448
For what?

470
00:26:57,916 --> 00:26:59,718
For all this hair to grow back.

471
00:26:59,785 --> 00:27:01,954
It'll grow back eventually, right?

472
00:27:02,020 --> 00:27:03,889
Still, it's such a relief.

473
00:27:05,157 --> 00:27:06,959
That's true, it really is.

474
00:27:08,293 --> 00:27:10,496
We don't have to meet in the next life.

475
00:27:11,296 --> 00:27:13,432
Now then, let's start over.

476
00:27:13,499 --> 00:27:14,366
Start what?

477
00:27:14,433 --> 00:27:15,901
I don't need another man.

478
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:18,937
So let's start your bucket list over.

479
00:27:20,506 --> 00:27:22,141
All right, next step.

480
00:27:22,207 --> 00:27:24,009
Are you ready?

481
00:27:24,076 --> 00:27:26,044
What?

482
00:27:26,111 --> 00:27:27,913
Can you hear my words?

483
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:32,918
My words that fell in love

484
00:27:33,886 --> 00:27:35,787
And can you see my eyes?

485
00:27:35,854 --> 00:27:40,726
My eyes that fell in love

486
00:27:41,927 --> 00:27:43,595
All day long

487
00:27:44,129 --> 00:27:46,465
Only the word love

488
00:27:46,532 --> 00:27:48,467
Lingers around me

489
00:27:55,374 --> 00:27:56,441
Hey.

490
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:59,444
I'd grown so attached to you guys.

491
00:27:59,945 --> 00:28:02,681
How can you leave so suddenly, jeez!

492
00:28:02,748 --> 00:28:04,449
Why are you doing this, sir?

493
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:06,051
I don't know, you punk!

494
00:28:06,118 --> 00:28:08,887
You don't know how I feel, you punk!

495
00:28:12,925 --> 00:28:14,960
Here he goes again, here he goes.

496
00:28:15,027 --> 00:28:17,396
He's way too soft-hearted.

497
00:28:18,130 --> 00:28:19,264
I'll put him to bed.

498
00:28:20,232 --> 00:28:22,668
Honey, get up. Let's go night-night.

499
00:28:22,734 --> 00:28:24,303
I'll sing you a lullaby.

500
00:28:26,138 --> 00:28:27,172
Should I sing one?

501
00:28:27,239 --> 00:28:29,174
Sure, I'll sing one for you.

502
00:28:29,241 --> 00:28:31,643
-I have to sleep.
-Come on, let's go.

503
00:28:31,710 --> 00:28:33,679
Hey, you guys just finish up…

504
00:28:33,745 --> 00:28:36,248
-Oh, goodness.
-Where are we going?

505
00:28:36,315 --> 00:28:37,849
Where? Are we going there?

506
00:28:37,916 --> 00:28:39,751
Um, no, to our room.

507
00:28:39,818 --> 00:28:40,953
Come to our room.

508
00:28:41,620 --> 00:28:43,956
He has such a unique drinking habit.

509
00:28:44,022 --> 00:28:45,357
Though he acts fine,

510
00:28:45,424 --> 00:28:47,859
he must be really sad deep down.

511
00:28:47,926 --> 00:28:50,495
We said we'd visit often, honestly.

512
00:28:54,733 --> 00:28:56,835
Where have you been?

513
00:28:56,902 --> 00:29:00,172
The world truly is a beautiful place!

514
00:29:00,239 --> 00:29:03,108
Being alive is such a blessing!

515
00:29:04,476 --> 00:29:07,045
What's with you? Were you dead before?

516
00:29:07,112 --> 00:29:10,782
Alas, you foolish mortals!
What could you possibly know?

517
00:29:10,849 --> 00:29:13,685
What's with the hat?
Did you shave your head?

518
00:29:14,486 --> 00:29:18,023
Don't ask me that. It breaks my heart.

519
00:29:18,090 --> 00:29:20,225
Hey, did you really shave your head?

520
00:29:20,292 --> 00:29:23,128
We have an album to make!
Why shave it bald, man?

521
00:29:23,195 --> 00:29:24,563
An album? What album?

522
00:29:24,630 --> 00:29:27,499
The agency came looking for us
to sign us right now!

523
00:29:27,566 --> 00:29:29,201
We can release an album now!

524
00:29:29,268 --> 00:29:32,938
Are you serious? For real? Really?

525
00:29:33,005 --> 00:29:34,239
Yes, I'm telling you.

526
00:29:34,306 --> 00:29:37,109
Our hard times are really over!

527
00:29:37,175 --> 00:29:38,977
Hard times are over!

528
00:29:39,044 --> 00:29:42,781
So many things happened overnight,
it's actually scaring me.

529
00:29:43,382 --> 00:29:45,250
I'm so glad I stayed alive.

530
00:29:45,317 --> 00:29:47,085
Thank you, God!

531
00:29:47,152 --> 00:29:49,821
No, thank you, cabbages! Thanks!

532
00:29:50,622 --> 00:29:51,823
Here, have a drink.

533
00:29:51,890 --> 00:29:53,725
Time to drink all night long!

534
00:29:53,792 --> 00:29:56,728
Can I actually drink now?

535
00:29:56,795 --> 00:29:58,330
I should go feed the cow.

536
00:29:58,397 --> 00:30:00,632
You guys enjoy and drink plenty.

537
00:30:23,388 --> 00:30:26,058
Why did you come out? Drink some more.

538
00:30:27,993 --> 00:30:30,896
I just came out for some fresh air.

539
00:30:36,201 --> 00:30:38,103
Thank you.

540
00:30:38,170 --> 00:30:39,037
For what?

541
00:30:39,104 --> 00:30:40,972
This is all thanks to you.

542
00:30:41,039 --> 00:30:44,576
Without you,
we wouldn't have made it this far.

543
00:30:44,643 --> 00:30:49,081
Go and give it your all.
This is what you wanted so badly.

544
00:30:49,147 --> 00:30:53,418
I'll be cheering for you from here,
so go out there and succeed.

545
00:30:53,485 --> 00:30:55,454
Make sure you top the music charts.

546
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:57,789
I will. Thank you so much.

547
00:30:57,856 --> 00:31:00,392
Why are you saying such cheesy things?

548
00:31:01,493 --> 00:31:04,796
When the album comes out,
make sure to send me a signed CD.

549
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:06,098
Concert tickets too?

550
00:31:06,798 --> 00:31:08,633
Of course I will, come on.

551
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:10,369
Me, I'll send the whole town's!

552
00:31:11,002 --> 00:31:12,671
Oh, seriously.

553
00:31:17,442 --> 00:31:19,311
Should I, should I help you?

554
00:31:19,811 --> 00:31:22,147
-I'm fine. Go in, it's cold.
-No, I'll help.

555
00:31:22,214 --> 00:31:23,882
I told you, just leave it.

556
00:31:23,949 --> 00:31:25,784
Give me that, I'll do it.

557
00:31:30,188 --> 00:31:32,357
Those fools, seriously.

558
00:31:39,798 --> 00:31:42,000
Life really is unpredictable.

559
00:31:42,067 --> 00:31:45,737
Who could've known
this would happen to us, right?

560
00:31:45,804 --> 00:31:49,307
-I know.
-It's goodbye to this cabbage field.

561
00:31:49,374 --> 00:31:53,678
We went through so much
and really grew attached to it.

562
00:31:58,116 --> 00:31:59,384
It's eight acres! Eight!

563
00:31:59,451 --> 00:32:01,686
It's eight acres! Eight acres!

564
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:04,089
Argh!

565
00:32:04,156 --> 00:32:05,290
All right!

566
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:18,403
Gosh, it's fine. Put it down.

567
00:32:18,470 --> 00:32:19,971
Ahh!

568
00:32:30,015 --> 00:32:34,319
So many crazy things happened, right?

569
00:32:35,587 --> 00:32:37,956
Anyway, what about all our cabbages?

570
00:32:38,023 --> 00:32:40,659
I'm donating them to people in need.

571
00:32:40,725 --> 00:32:45,564
We sweated blood to grow them,
so it's nice to put them to good use.

572
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:47,466
Good thinking.

573
00:32:48,066 --> 00:32:50,101
Anyway…

574
00:32:51,503 --> 00:32:54,306
is this goodbye to this town now too?

575
00:32:54,906 --> 00:32:57,108
We grew so close to the villagers too.

576
00:32:57,175 --> 00:32:58,043
I know.

577
00:32:58,477 --> 00:33:02,881
Now that we're actually leaving,
my heart feels a little heavy.

578
00:33:04,483 --> 00:33:07,819
Let's head back
and help the villagers with their work.

579
00:33:07,886 --> 00:33:10,689
We have a few days left.
Doing that'll ease my mind.

580
00:33:10,755 --> 00:33:13,325
Okay, let's do that. Let's go.

581
00:33:13,391 --> 00:33:16,161
Um, you two go on ahead.
I need to talk to Min-gi.

582
00:33:16,228 --> 00:33:18,230
Okay, go ahead and talk.

583
00:33:24,035 --> 00:33:25,737
Talk about what?

584
00:33:25,804 --> 00:33:27,639
You know, I…

585
00:33:29,841 --> 00:33:32,811
I really want Yun-hui to be happy.

586
00:33:32,878 --> 00:33:35,280
-And?
-But…

587
00:33:36,314 --> 00:33:39,251
I realized I can't do that for her.

588
00:33:39,317 --> 00:33:40,919
Someone can make her happy,

589
00:33:40,986 --> 00:33:43,154
only one person in this world,

590
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:48,026
and unfortunately, it's you.

591
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:50,395
What?

592
00:33:50,462 --> 00:33:52,864
Do you really not know,
or are you pretending?

593
00:33:52,931 --> 00:33:55,734
You already know how Yun-hui feels.

594
00:34:03,341 --> 00:34:04,309
What about you?

595
00:34:05,443 --> 00:34:06,878
Well…

596
00:34:08,847 --> 00:34:10,482
I don't really know

597
00:34:11,716 --> 00:34:13,351
what this feeling is.

598
00:34:13,418 --> 00:34:16,354
Fools often confuse pity with love.

599
00:34:17,188 --> 00:34:18,957
Think carefully

600
00:34:19,024 --> 00:34:20,992
about who's on your mind the most.

601
00:34:21,059 --> 00:34:23,895
When she cries, your heart aches too.

602
00:34:23,962 --> 00:34:28,033
When she smiles, even your mood lifts.

603
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,769
When it's hard, you lean on her.

604
00:34:30,835 --> 00:34:33,838
Who gives you strength
just by being by your side?

605
00:34:33,905 --> 00:34:35,674
Think hard about who that is.

606
00:34:36,808 --> 00:34:38,810
You'll miss your chance if you stall.

607
00:34:38,877 --> 00:34:41,379
I was so annoyed,
I wasn't going to tell you.

608
00:34:42,948 --> 00:34:44,816
But I'm doing this for Yun-hui.

609
00:34:44,883 --> 00:34:46,685
Not for your sake, mind you.

610
00:34:46,751 --> 00:34:48,553
I'm leaving.

611
00:35:07,839 --> 00:35:09,407
It's here! It's still here.

612
00:35:09,474 --> 00:35:11,376
Wow, this is still here.

613
00:35:12,043 --> 00:35:14,379
Wait, was this your doing too?

614
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:27,959
Hang in there. It's not over yet.

615
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:30,895
I'll find a way no matter what.

616
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:33,131
So don't worry.

617
00:35:51,850 --> 00:35:54,185
Min-ho, cheer up.

618
00:35:54,252 --> 00:35:57,422
Min-gyeong said
she'll come down once a week.

619
00:35:57,489 --> 00:36:00,025
Let's go buy tasty food at the market.

620
00:36:00,091 --> 00:36:01,760
I'll make the tastiest food.

621
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:03,628
What would you like to eat?

622
00:36:06,731 --> 00:36:08,299
I'll make it for you.

623
00:36:10,702 --> 00:36:11,569
Okay?

624
00:36:26,151 --> 00:36:28,420
What are you doing here?

625
00:36:42,067 --> 00:36:44,135
Min-ho.

626
00:36:44,202 --> 00:36:46,204
You were really hurt, weren't you?

627
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:53,445
Dad is so sorry.

628
00:36:54,646 --> 00:36:56,114
I was wrong.

629
00:36:58,717 --> 00:37:00,752
My sweet Min-ho,

630
00:37:01,453 --> 00:37:04,022
can I give you just one hug?

631
00:37:11,796 --> 00:37:13,565
I'm so sorry.

632
00:37:14,833 --> 00:37:16,968
I was so wrong.

633
00:37:17,035 --> 00:37:19,070
You were wrong.

634
00:37:19,137 --> 00:37:20,605
I'm sorry.

635
00:37:25,677 --> 00:37:27,512
Don't cry.

636
00:37:36,788 --> 00:37:41,493
I know it's shameless, but I'll try.

637
00:37:42,093 --> 00:37:46,331
Won't you give me a chance
to make it up to you starting now?

638
00:38:18,429 --> 00:38:22,700
That damn bastard!
He sure showed up nice and early!

639
00:38:23,468 --> 00:38:25,770
I can understand how he felt too.

640
00:38:25,837 --> 00:38:29,340
If it were me,
I'd have been so panicked and scared.

641
00:38:30,008 --> 00:38:32,844
So what are you going to do now?

642
00:38:34,179 --> 00:38:35,780
I'm not sure either.

643
00:38:35,847 --> 00:38:36,948
What about Min-ho?

644
00:38:37,015 --> 00:38:39,117
He just bawled his eyes out.

645
00:38:39,184 --> 00:38:40,585
How could he not?

646
00:38:40,652 --> 00:38:44,222
That little boy held it all in
so he wouldn't upset you,

647
00:38:44,289 --> 00:38:45,657
and it all burst out.

648
00:38:46,791 --> 00:38:51,196
I hope you work things out with him.

649
00:38:51,262 --> 00:38:54,499
Stop struggling all by yourself now.

650
00:38:54,566 --> 00:38:56,201
I want you to live happily.

651
00:38:56,968 --> 00:38:58,403
That's right.

652
00:38:58,469 --> 00:39:02,373
Even for Min-ho's sake, he needs a dad.

653
00:39:02,440 --> 00:39:04,642
It's not something to force on her.

654
00:39:04,709 --> 00:39:07,178
Think about Yun-hui's feelings, too.

655
00:39:08,279 --> 00:39:11,549
Yun-hui, we…

656
00:39:11,616 --> 00:39:15,086
are unconditionally on your side,
no matter what you decide.

657
00:39:15,153 --> 00:39:17,455
So decide for yourself what is best.

658
00:39:17,522 --> 00:39:20,925
What matters most is your happiness.

659
00:39:25,530 --> 00:39:30,034
But isn't this good for Yun-hui?

660
00:39:30,101 --> 00:39:32,737
Right, it's better for Min-ho, too.

661
00:39:32,804 --> 00:39:35,240
True, he's super famous and rich, too.

662
00:39:35,306 --> 00:39:37,976
Yun-hui's set for life in one shot.

663
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:39,911
You're talking nonsense, kid.

664
00:39:39,978 --> 00:39:41,713
No, I was just…

665
00:39:42,947 --> 00:39:45,183
I mean, honestly, it worked out well.

666
00:39:45,250 --> 00:39:47,218
Yun-hui suffered so much all alone,

667
00:39:47,285 --> 00:39:49,320
raising her kid like that, huh?

668
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:51,522
Isn't luxury with a rich husband good?

669
00:39:51,589 --> 00:39:53,458
Shut up and go to sleep.

670
00:39:54,158 --> 00:39:56,160
You're so snappy for no reason.

671
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:58,062
Oh, gosh, seriously.

672
00:39:58,129 --> 00:39:59,964
Someone turn off the light.

673
00:40:12,543 --> 00:40:14,946
Tomorrow's the day you head back up.

674
00:40:15,013 --> 00:40:16,848
Did everyone get ready okay?

675
00:40:17,749 --> 00:40:21,319
Yes, we donated all the cabbages,
and now we just have to pack.

676
00:40:21,386 --> 00:40:23,388
Do you even have anything to pack?

677
00:40:23,454 --> 00:40:25,790
You came here empty-handed.

678
00:40:29,460 --> 00:40:32,897
Thank you for the meal.
I will go pick up Min-ho.

679
00:40:41,306 --> 00:40:43,775
She must have a lot on her mind.

680
00:40:43,841 --> 00:40:46,010
Of course she does.

681
00:40:46,744 --> 00:40:51,683
Gosh, I really can't tell
whether this is a good or bad thing.

682
00:40:55,954 --> 00:40:57,121
He is dribbling now!

683
00:40:57,188 --> 00:41:00,625
He dribbles and shoots!
Oh, his seventh shot! Oh!

684
00:41:00,692 --> 00:41:02,627
-It's a goal!
-Goal!

685
00:41:02,694 --> 00:41:04,362
Again, again!

686
00:41:06,831 --> 00:41:09,167
-Mom!
-Hey, Min-ho.

687
00:41:10,768 --> 00:41:12,170
Did you have fun playing?

688
00:41:12,236 --> 00:41:13,905
Yes.

689
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:17,508
But what brings you here again?

690
00:41:17,575 --> 00:41:19,677
I came because I missed Min-ho.

691
00:41:20,345 --> 00:41:22,547
Why? Am I making you uncomfortable?

692
00:41:22,613 --> 00:41:25,583
No, it's not necessarily like that.

693
00:41:25,650 --> 00:41:28,419
Even if you're uncomfortable,
I'll come every day.

694
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:30,621
I'll keep coming until you accept me.

695
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:34,192
Yun-hui, I have something to tell you.

696
00:41:35,126 --> 00:41:36,995
I'm going abroad again next month.

697
00:41:37,061 --> 00:41:40,198
-Let's go together then.
-What?

698
00:41:40,264 --> 00:41:42,066
You don't need to prepare a thing.

699
00:41:42,133 --> 00:41:43,868
I've prepared everything.

700
00:41:43,935 --> 00:41:45,303
So come with me, Yun-hui.

701
00:41:46,104 --> 00:41:48,673
Let's start fresh somewhere new.

702
00:41:48,740 --> 00:41:50,408
Together as a family.

703
00:41:50,942 --> 00:41:52,477
I asked Min-ho.

704
00:41:52,543 --> 00:41:54,612
Min-ho says he's fine if you are.

705
00:41:55,179 --> 00:41:56,848
What do you think?

706
00:42:00,251 --> 00:42:01,252
All right.

707
00:42:01,319 --> 00:42:04,622
You still have time, so think it over.

708
00:42:05,723 --> 00:42:07,892
Mister, hurry up and come over!

709
00:42:09,660 --> 00:42:11,329
Okay!

710
00:42:43,127 --> 00:42:45,263
What are you doing here?

711
00:42:45,997 --> 00:42:48,132
Is something wrong?

712
00:42:49,133 --> 00:42:50,668
No, it's nothing.

713
00:42:50,735 --> 00:42:54,138
Come on, I can tell it's not nothing.

714
00:42:54,205 --> 00:42:56,908
Talk to me. I told you, right?

715
00:42:56,974 --> 00:43:00,044
Even if I can't fix it, I can listen.

716
00:43:00,111 --> 00:43:02,780
Go on, tell me.

717
00:43:03,448 --> 00:43:07,685
Could it be about Min-ho's dad?

718
00:43:09,821 --> 00:43:11,789
He wants us to go abroad together.

719
00:43:13,691 --> 00:43:15,326
What?

720
00:43:16,627 --> 00:43:18,196
Oh, really?

721
00:43:20,731 --> 00:43:22,400
Min-gi.

722
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:25,303
Should I go with him?

723
00:43:27,305 --> 00:43:30,274
No, I don't want you to go.

724
00:43:36,948 --> 00:43:41,018
I mean, if you leave,
I'll have no one left to tease.

725
00:43:41,085 --> 00:43:44,689
But for Min-ho's sake,
isn't it better to have his dad there?

726
00:43:44,755 --> 00:43:47,425
And for you too, right?

727
00:43:48,926 --> 00:43:50,695
This is really tough.

728
00:43:52,964 --> 00:43:55,566
All right, I've heard you out.

729
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:58,636
The decision is up to you.

730
00:43:58,703 --> 00:44:01,005
Whatever you decide,

731
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:04,342
your feelings are what matter most.

732
00:44:06,410 --> 00:44:08,146
I'll get going.

733
00:44:10,281 --> 00:44:11,916
Gosh.

734
00:44:37,041 --> 00:44:38,976
Are you really leaving like this?

735
00:44:39,043 --> 00:44:41,145
What will you do if Yun-hui leaves?

736
00:44:41,212 --> 00:44:43,514
It's not like that's a bad thing.

737
00:44:44,615 --> 00:44:46,817
Whether it's for Min-ho

738
00:44:46,884 --> 00:44:49,554
or for her, it's better that way.

739
00:44:51,155 --> 00:44:53,324
You've seen way too many movies.

740
00:44:53,391 --> 00:44:56,027
That doesn't make you look cool.

741
00:45:05,236 --> 00:45:07,338
Thank you for everything.

742
00:45:07,405 --> 00:45:09,640
All right, come visit sometime.

743
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:10,942
Yes, sir.

744
00:45:11,008 --> 00:45:13,911
Get home safe, and don't catch a cold.

745
00:45:13,978 --> 00:45:15,813
We will, Yeong-sik.

746
00:45:16,347 --> 00:45:19,617
Why are you crying?
It's not like we'll never meet again.

747
00:45:19,684 --> 00:45:23,521
I'm not crying.
Water's just coming out of my eyes.

748
00:45:23,588 --> 00:45:27,391
Sir, ma'am, thank you for everything.

749
00:45:27,458 --> 00:45:29,427
We'll come visit often.

750
00:45:29,493 --> 00:45:32,096
Don't ever come back.
I'm sick of seeing you.

751
00:45:32,163 --> 00:45:34,432
-Oh, dear.
-Oh, man.

752
00:45:34,498 --> 00:45:36,234
Eat this on the way.

753
00:45:36,300 --> 00:45:37,702
Oh? What is this?

754
00:45:37,768 --> 00:45:41,038
It's seaweed chocolate fondue.
You really liked this.

755
00:45:42,306 --> 00:45:46,310
Yes, thank you so much. I'll enjoy it.

756
00:45:47,845 --> 00:45:50,781
By the way, I don't see Man-gu.

757
00:45:57,088 --> 00:45:58,723
Man-gu!

758
00:46:03,294 --> 00:46:05,263
Here, take it.

759
00:46:05,763 --> 00:46:06,831
But you bought this.

760
00:46:06,897 --> 00:46:08,766
How can I drive this in the cold?

761
00:46:09,834 --> 00:46:11,369
I'm sick of it, that's why.

762
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:13,037
I'm buying a better one.

763
00:46:13,104 --> 00:46:14,472
So just take it.

764
00:46:16,173 --> 00:46:17,208
Thank you.

765
00:46:17,275 --> 00:46:20,278
And call me often,

766
00:46:20,344 --> 00:46:24,915
and message me sometimes, you punks!

767
00:46:25,950 --> 00:46:29,253
Yes, I'll call and message you often.

768
00:46:30,721 --> 00:46:32,623
Um, I have a favor to ask.

769
00:46:32,690 --> 00:46:33,624
Yes.

770
00:46:33,691 --> 00:46:36,160
Sing a wedding song for me later.

771
00:46:36,227 --> 00:46:37,795
A wedding song? What wedding?

772
00:46:44,869 --> 00:46:46,103
Oh!

773
00:46:46,170 --> 00:46:48,172
I got it, I got it.

774
00:46:48,239 --> 00:46:49,640
-Call me.
-Sure, call me.

775
00:46:49,707 --> 00:46:52,443
-I'll get going now.
-Man-gu, don't cry.

776
00:46:52,510 --> 00:46:54,211
Thank you so much.

777
00:47:03,020 --> 00:47:05,156
Min-ho, I'm leaving now.

778
00:47:05,222 --> 00:47:07,358
You have to come visit often.

779
00:47:07,425 --> 00:47:09,593
I will, so don't cry.

780
00:47:10,795 --> 00:47:12,763
I'm leaving, Yun-hui.

781
00:47:12,830 --> 00:47:14,799
Come on, stop frowning.

782
00:47:14,865 --> 00:47:16,600
It makes you look even uglier.

783
00:47:16,667 --> 00:47:18,636
Seriously? Jeez.

784
00:47:18,703 --> 00:47:21,739
You're prettiest when you're annoyed.

785
00:47:22,740 --> 00:47:24,475
I'm leaving.

786
00:47:24,542 --> 00:47:26,811
I'm heading out.

787
00:47:31,148 --> 00:47:33,250
Sang-deuk, don't cry!

788
00:47:33,317 --> 00:47:34,385
Have a safe trip!

789
00:47:34,452 --> 00:47:36,087
Thank you for everything!

790
00:47:39,357 --> 00:47:40,491
Hey.

791
00:47:40,558 --> 00:47:42,727
Are you really okay leaving like this?

792
00:47:42,793 --> 00:47:44,428
Won't you confess your love?

793
00:47:49,600 --> 00:47:50,901
I already did, man.

794
00:47:50,968 --> 00:47:52,636
In my heart.

795
00:47:53,804 --> 00:47:56,407
I'll just leave the rest up to heaven.

796
00:47:58,909 --> 00:47:59,977
Shall we get going?

797
00:48:00,044 --> 00:48:01,712
Let's go.

798
00:48:15,726 --> 00:48:19,230
MODERN FARMER

799
00:48:30,341 --> 00:48:34,578
Yun-hui, are you all packed?

800
00:48:34,645 --> 00:48:36,013
Yes, I'm almost packed.

801
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:38,215
Gosh.

802
00:48:40,518 --> 00:48:42,653
Why do you look so down?

803
00:48:44,655 --> 00:48:47,591
I'm not even sure if this is right.

804
00:48:49,326 --> 00:48:51,862
Yun-hui, when things get complicated,

805
00:48:51,929 --> 00:48:54,832
keeping it simple is the way to go.

806
00:48:55,466 --> 00:48:57,835
All you want is for Min-ho to be happy.

807
00:48:58,869 --> 00:48:59,970
That's true.

808
00:49:00,037 --> 00:49:02,373
But for Min-ho to be happy,

809
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:05,676
you need to be happy first, Yun-hui.

810
00:49:05,743 --> 00:49:08,546
How can Min-ho be happy if you aren't?

811
00:49:08,612 --> 00:49:10,648
Isn't that right?

812
00:49:10,714 --> 00:49:12,383
You're right.

813
00:49:12,983 --> 00:49:15,119
I'll think it over carefully, Aunt.

814
00:49:15,186 --> 00:49:16,854
Okay.

815
00:49:16,921 --> 00:49:21,192
I trust you'll make the right choice.

816
00:49:21,258 --> 00:49:23,427
Thank you.

817
00:50:00,431 --> 00:50:03,100
-Here.
-What is this?

818
00:50:03,167 --> 00:50:05,603
They say this is great for anti-aging.

819
00:50:05,669 --> 00:50:08,572
You have all those fine wrinkles
right under your eyes.

820
00:50:08,639 --> 00:50:10,174
You should put it on early.

821
00:50:10,241 --> 00:50:13,110
Who knows?
Some blind fool might fall for you.

822
00:50:21,051 --> 00:50:24,054
MIN-GI ♥ YUN-HUI

823
00:50:41,272 --> 00:50:42,907
Hey, hold on.

824
00:50:44,842 --> 00:50:46,710
No need to be nervous.

825
00:50:46,777 --> 00:50:49,046
We dreamed of this forever.
No shaking now!

826
00:50:49,113 --> 00:50:50,848
Who are we?

827
00:50:50,915 --> 00:50:54,351
We're the battle-hardened veterans
who grew 100,000 cabbages!

828
00:50:54,418 --> 00:50:56,353
Compared to that, this is nothing.

829
00:50:56,987 --> 00:50:58,956
Stay sharp, everyone.

830
00:51:01,392 --> 00:51:03,661
Let's blow everyone away! Okay?

831
00:51:03,727 --> 00:51:04,595
Okay!

832
00:51:04,662 --> 00:51:06,597
-Let's do this!

833
00:51:29,720 --> 00:51:31,555
-That was insane!
-I know!

834
00:51:31,622 --> 00:51:32,489
Great job!

835
00:51:32,556 --> 00:51:33,424
Missed a chord?

836
00:51:33,490 --> 00:51:34,358
That's right.

837
00:51:34,425 --> 00:51:36,026
No, I did, but nobody noticed.

838
00:51:36,093 --> 00:51:37,828
-No way.
-It went over smoothly.

839
00:51:37,895 --> 00:51:40,264
It showed all over your face today.

840
00:51:40,331 --> 00:51:42,333
The crowd was already mesmerized.

841
00:51:42,399 --> 00:51:45,569
Honestly, we're way better
than FTISLAND now.

842
00:51:45,636 --> 00:51:47,871
Get your lines ready.
Fans will swarm us!

843
00:51:47,938 --> 00:51:49,540
Go on. I'll be right back.

844
00:51:49,607 --> 00:51:51,275
Okay, go on, but hurry back.

845
00:51:51,342 --> 00:51:53,410
The crowd completely lost their minds!

846
00:51:53,477 --> 00:51:56,146
We need our lines ready.
The crowd will swarm us!

847
00:51:56,213 --> 00:51:58,282
-Our fans!
-Hurry back!

848
00:52:05,089 --> 00:52:09,193
Min-gi was really cool, right, Mom?

849
00:52:09,259 --> 00:52:12,630
He really was.
He looked like a whole new person.

850
00:52:13,397 --> 00:52:15,332
He looked so at peace, too.

851
00:52:15,399 --> 00:52:20,270
Will Min-gi come visit our house?

852
00:52:20,337 --> 00:52:24,575
Well, Min-gi is busy,
so he probably can't come.

853
00:52:24,642 --> 00:52:26,777
Don't be too disappointed, okay?

854
00:52:26,844 --> 00:52:31,115
Then we won't get to see Min-gi?

855
00:52:31,181 --> 00:52:33,651
Why? Does that make you sad?

856
00:52:42,493 --> 00:52:43,894
Huh?

857
00:52:46,397 --> 00:52:50,501
YUN-HYEOK ♡

858
00:53:01,845 --> 00:53:05,983
YUN-HUI ♡ I'M SORRY

859
00:53:45,355 --> 00:53:47,991
ONE YEAR LATER

860
00:53:52,963 --> 00:53:54,898
Darn it, I need to keep it steady.

861
00:53:56,734 --> 00:53:58,602
This isn't it.

862
00:54:00,738 --> 00:54:03,273
Hey, son! I'm here too!

863
00:54:03,340 --> 00:54:05,776
-Did you have fun?
-Yes.

864
00:54:05,843 --> 00:54:07,177
I asked you to help out,

865
00:54:07,244 --> 00:54:09,379
and you just lazed around goofing off?

866
00:54:09,446 --> 00:54:12,483
Lazing around? I was writing a song!

867
00:54:12,549 --> 00:54:14,685
Oh, please. Why write a song? Why?

868
00:54:14,752 --> 00:54:18,222
Your one album totally flopped,
so why are you writing a song?

869
00:54:18,288 --> 00:54:20,891
It flopped,
so I'm making a second album!

870
00:54:20,958 --> 00:54:22,126
To restore my honor!

871
00:54:22,192 --> 00:54:24,895
Restore your honor? Yeah, right.

872
00:54:24,962 --> 00:54:26,530
Just quit while you're ahead.

873
00:54:26,597 --> 00:54:28,999
"A head" is for counting cabbages.

874
00:54:29,066 --> 00:54:30,567
I'd rather die than quit!

875
00:54:31,435 --> 00:54:34,872
It's better to die
than live without passion.

876
00:54:34,938 --> 00:54:37,107
Don't you know Kurt Cobain?

877
00:54:37,174 --> 00:54:40,377
It's better to live alone
than live with a useless husband.

878
00:54:40,444 --> 00:54:41,979
Don't you know Kang Yun-hui?

879
00:54:42,045 --> 00:54:43,881
How do you never back down?

880
00:54:43,947 --> 00:54:45,182
Oh, enough of that.

881
00:54:45,249 --> 00:54:48,185
Go get the money you lent Han-cheol.

882
00:54:48,252 --> 00:54:50,087
We're short on living expenses!

883
00:54:50,154 --> 00:54:52,489
How can I ask a friend to pay me back?

884
00:54:52,556 --> 00:54:54,324
I know they're struggling too.

885
00:54:54,391 --> 00:54:58,462
Gosh, I can't take this anymore!

886
00:55:02,332 --> 00:55:04,368
Honey, how about this one?

887
00:55:04,434 --> 00:55:06,570
Oh, it's so pretty!

888
00:55:06,637 --> 00:55:09,173
Come on, just pick anything.

889
00:55:09,239 --> 00:55:11,508
These are for your baby sibling!

890
00:55:11,575 --> 00:55:13,043
How can I not be picky?

891
00:55:13,110 --> 00:55:16,346
I can't face the town.
I'm just dying of embarrassment!

892
00:55:16,413 --> 00:55:19,583
How can my own sibling
be younger than my son?

893
00:55:19,650 --> 00:55:21,318
Will he live to see college?

894
00:55:21,385 --> 00:55:24,221
We can just get his will in advance.

895
00:55:26,523 --> 00:55:28,592
Why, you little brats!

896
00:55:28,659 --> 00:55:31,128
Gosh, and I call you two my sisters!

897
00:55:31,195 --> 00:55:33,430
Hey, how long will you just look?

898
00:55:33,497 --> 00:55:34,798
Hurry and pick! Hurry!

899
00:55:34,865 --> 00:55:36,867
Seriously.

900
00:55:36,934 --> 00:55:40,003
Don't rush me!
Don't you know the customer is king?

901
00:55:43,874 --> 00:55:46,877
Honey, we're in big trouble.
What should we do?

902
00:55:46,944 --> 00:55:47,811
Why? Why?

903
00:55:47,878 --> 00:55:50,848
They're raising the shop rent
by ten million won at once.

904
00:55:50,914 --> 00:55:51,949
Ten million won?

905
00:55:52,015 --> 00:55:54,251
Where do we get ten million won now?

906
00:55:54,318 --> 00:55:55,552
Darn it.

907
00:55:55,619 --> 00:55:57,421
I can't believe this.

908
00:56:00,290 --> 00:56:04,161
Another collect call.
It has to be Ki-jun. Definitely Ki-jun.

909
00:56:04,928 --> 00:56:06,363
Hello?

910
00:56:06,430 --> 00:56:08,031
I knew you'd call, punk.

911
00:56:08,098 --> 00:56:09,933
What is it this time?

912
00:56:10,000 --> 00:56:12,769
What? I have no money, you jerk!

913
00:56:12,836 --> 00:56:14,204
Then why go to Damn-bian?

914
00:56:14,805 --> 00:56:17,507
YANBIAN

915
00:56:21,545 --> 00:56:24,081
I don't know why getting by is so hard.

916
00:56:24,147 --> 00:56:25,983
Tell me about it.

917
00:56:26,950 --> 00:56:29,953
Bul-ja, Bul-ja, what are you doing?

918
00:56:33,257 --> 00:56:35,959
You've had it rough.
Watch out for crackdowns.

919
00:56:37,461 --> 00:56:39,029
Crackdowns? Who is he?

920
00:56:39,630 --> 00:56:41,698
He's an illegal immigrant from Korea.

921
00:56:41,765 --> 00:56:43,567
An illegal immigrant from Korea?

922
00:56:43,634 --> 00:56:46,270
Well, he came here on a tourist visa,

923
00:56:46,336 --> 00:56:49,740
partied away, not knowing it expired,

924
00:56:49,806 --> 00:56:51,775
and ended up in that pathetic state.

925
00:56:51,842 --> 00:56:54,678
How careless can he be
to let that happen to him?

926
00:56:54,745 --> 00:56:56,847
Anyway, this is a secret.

927
00:56:56,914 --> 00:56:58,916
You have to take it to your grave.

928
00:57:02,619 --> 00:57:05,756
-Honey.
-Oh, Hwa-ran.

929
00:57:05,822 --> 00:57:07,658
Why come out in your condition?

930
00:57:07,724 --> 00:57:11,828
I came out because I was worried.
Did you borrow the money?

931
00:57:11,895 --> 00:57:15,699
No, it seems Han-cheol is having
a hard time lately too.

932
00:57:15,766 --> 00:57:18,435
Should I try asking Hyeok for a loan?

933
00:57:20,103 --> 00:57:22,673
Hey, man, I don't have any money.

934
00:57:22,739 --> 00:57:25,509
I messed up too,
and running from Dad is killing me.

935
00:57:25,575 --> 00:57:28,478
Stop talking nonsense.
I have patients to see. Hang up.

936
00:57:29,513 --> 00:57:31,515
Don't you keep the IV in these days?

937
00:57:33,317 --> 00:57:35,819
Hey, Hyeok, what happened to Grandpa?

938
00:57:35,886 --> 00:57:38,188
He's fine.
He ate too many chocolate bars,

939
00:57:38,255 --> 00:57:41,124
so his blood sugar just spiked a bit.
Don't worry.

940
00:57:41,191 --> 00:57:43,994
And please don't let him eat
chocolate bars anymore.

941
00:57:44,061 --> 00:57:47,297
No way, you brat! I'd rather die
than quit chocolate bars!

942
00:57:47,364 --> 00:57:50,600
Father, please give up
those chocolate bars already.

943
00:57:50,667 --> 00:57:54,604
And aren't you embarrassed
in front of your great-granddaughter?

944
00:57:55,973 --> 00:57:58,342
I'm fine.
Grandpa has to eat chocolate bars

945
00:57:58,408 --> 00:58:01,211
so that I can eat the almonds!

946
00:58:01,278 --> 00:58:04,648
Did you actually eat
the almonds Grandpa gave you?

947
00:58:04,715 --> 00:58:06,883
Yes, why?

948
00:58:06,950 --> 00:58:10,354
Don't eat those anymore.
Never ever eat them, got it?

949
00:58:10,420 --> 00:58:12,422
Pinky promise me.

950
00:58:13,156 --> 00:58:15,826
With so much else to eat,
why would you eat those?

951
00:58:15,892 --> 00:58:18,061
MODERN FARMER

952
00:58:18,128 --> 00:58:20,764
-Mmm, looks delicious!
-That looks so good.

953
00:58:20,831 --> 00:58:22,933
Seriously, you've gone way too far!

954
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:24,668
Look, even if our album flopped,

955
00:58:24,735 --> 00:58:26,436
how can you make it a pot stand?

956
00:58:26,503 --> 00:58:29,106
Be glad this thing has any use, okay?

957
00:58:29,172 --> 00:58:30,941
What else is this good for? What?

958
00:58:31,008 --> 00:58:32,876
Unbelievable, seriously.

959
00:58:32,943 --> 00:58:35,078
And why is it always ramen? Ramen?

960
00:58:35,145 --> 00:58:36,780
Take a cooking class, please.

961
00:58:36,847 --> 00:58:39,316
If you don't want it, don't eat it.

962
00:58:39,383 --> 00:58:41,318
Whining? You don't earn your keep.

963
00:58:41,385 --> 00:58:45,222
Excuse me?
How can you look down on me like that?

964
00:58:45,288 --> 00:58:46,790
What if our second album

965
00:58:46,857 --> 00:58:48,091
blows up? What then?

966
00:58:48,158 --> 00:58:50,227
A second album? Don't make me laugh.

967
00:58:50,293 --> 00:58:53,030
Who says they'll release
another album for you?

968
00:58:53,096 --> 00:58:55,699
Wait and see. No matter what it takes,

969
00:58:55,766 --> 00:58:57,868
I'll definitely release a second album.

970
00:58:57,934 --> 00:58:59,903
In other news, on our West Coast,

971
00:58:59,970 --> 00:59:02,839
schools of tuna appeared,
bringing a fishing boom.

972
00:59:02,906 --> 00:59:04,441
The tuna spotted this time

973
00:59:04,508 --> 00:59:06,209
are known as top-quality tuna,

974
00:59:06,276 --> 00:59:08,078
and depending on their weight,

975
00:59:08,145 --> 00:59:09,846
each fetches ten million won,

976
00:59:09,913 --> 00:59:11,515
according to reports.

977
00:59:11,581 --> 00:59:13,050
What?

978
00:59:13,116 --> 00:59:16,253
Ten million won per fish?

979
00:59:17,187 --> 00:59:19,356
Catching just ten is 100 million won.

980
00:59:19,423 --> 00:59:21,792
And if I catch 100 of them…

981
00:59:22,559 --> 00:59:23,860
one billion won!

982
00:59:26,029 --> 00:59:28,565
-What's wrong with you?
-What?

983
00:59:28,632 --> 00:59:29,900
No, it's nothing.

984
00:59:29,966 --> 00:59:31,368
Uh, I'll go make a call.

985
00:59:31,435 --> 00:59:34,171
Excuse me, I'll go make a quick call.

986
00:59:36,907 --> 00:59:38,842
Hey, it's me.

987
00:59:38,909 --> 00:59:40,877
Listen to me carefully right now.

988
00:59:40,944 --> 00:59:43,313
Because this is a historic, historic,

989
00:59:43,380 --> 00:59:45,315
jaw-droppingly massive event!

990
00:59:58,995 --> 01:00:00,630
Hey, Min-gi!

991
01:00:01,631 --> 01:00:04,868
If we catch tuna, can we really
release our second album?

992
01:00:04,935 --> 01:00:06,970
Of course we can, man!

993
01:00:07,037 --> 01:00:09,706
Just ten! We only need to catch ten!

994
01:00:09,773 --> 01:00:11,641
Really?

995
01:00:11,708 --> 01:00:15,312
Hey, can guys like us even catch tuna?

996
01:00:15,378 --> 01:00:17,414
Of course, man!

997
01:00:17,481 --> 01:00:18,682
Tuna's no big deal.

998
01:00:18,748 --> 01:00:21,451
Put an earthworm on a rod,
dip the worm in the sea,

999
01:00:21,518 --> 01:00:23,086
and once it chomps the bait,

1000
01:00:23,153 --> 01:00:25,822
just reel it right in and scoop it up!

1001
01:00:25,889 --> 01:00:28,725
Think I can't do that?
We can do it all. Don't worry.

1002
01:00:28,792 --> 01:00:30,627
Feels like I'm taking the bait…

1003
01:00:30,694 --> 01:00:32,429
Okay, okay, let's go, let's go!

1004
01:00:32,496 --> 01:00:36,433
Hey, but can we really catch a tuna
with such a tiny fishing rod?

1005
01:00:36,500 --> 01:00:38,301
Do big guys always fight better?

1006
01:00:38,368 --> 01:00:40,971
Small is fine if you have the skill.
Just skill.

1007
01:00:41,037 --> 01:00:42,572
Shouldn't the net be bigger?

1008
01:00:42,639 --> 01:00:44,808
Hey, who cares about the net?

1009
01:00:44,875 --> 01:00:47,711
Once it chomps down,
all four of us can team up

1010
01:00:47,777 --> 01:00:49,412
and yank it right out.

1011
01:00:49,479 --> 01:00:51,214
I heard big ones top 300 kg.

1012
01:00:51,281 --> 01:00:54,151
A weightlifter lifts 200 kg alone.
Don't worry, man.

1013
01:00:54,217 --> 01:00:55,986
Well, that's true.

1014
01:01:00,290 --> 01:01:03,560
Tuna, wait for us! Here we come!

1015
01:01:04,961 --> 01:01:07,697
Tuna, here we come!

1016
01:01:07,764 --> 01:01:09,065
Bring it on!

1017
01:01:12,569 --> 01:01:14,938
Hey, what is that? What is that?

1018
01:01:15,005 --> 01:01:16,640
Isn't that a tuna?

1019
01:01:16,706 --> 01:01:19,743
Guys, it's a tuna! A tuna is flying!

1020
01:01:21,645 --> 01:01:23,380
TO OUR MODERN FARMER VIEWERS,

1021
01:01:23,446 --> 01:01:25,348
WE SINCERELY THANK YOU.

1022
01:01:25,415 --> 01:01:26,883
Uh, this is embarrassing.

1023
01:01:26,950 --> 01:01:28,385
If you endure and run on…

1024
01:01:28,451 --> 01:01:29,619
Go, Modern Farmer!

1025
01:01:29,686 --> 01:01:31,488
Can we do it like this too?

1026
01:01:31,555 --> 01:01:34,324
This is Bonghwa,
where the best pine mushrooms grow.

1027
01:01:41,164 --> 01:01:43,200
This lets us harvest the cabbages.

1028
01:01:43,266 --> 01:01:45,402
And the cabbages harvested this way

1029
01:01:45,468 --> 01:01:48,505
are finally reborn
as delicious pickled cabbage.

1030
01:01:48,572 --> 01:01:50,907
Well, something like that.

1031
01:01:50,974 --> 01:01:52,909
IT'S OKAY, IT'S OKAY

1032
01:01:52,976 --> 01:01:54,778
Thank you for all your hard work.

1033
01:01:54,844 --> 01:01:57,881
-Modern Farmer!
-Let's go!

1034
01:01:57,948 --> 01:01:59,416
Great work, everyone.

1035
01:01:59,482 --> 01:02:01,685
Great work, everyone!
